Chapter 2 – The Irreversibility of Knowledge

Media revolutions—oral → writing → print → computation → artificial intelligence—compress the global growth of declarative knowledge and begin to digitize procedural knowledge. However, the physical capital constraints encoded in the O‑ring model (§5.4) prevent complete transfer; digital‑transfer ceilings τ_i for heavy industrial nodes remain low.

